{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Without end.</b> Though he is wise, all the living will not rejoice in him, for the judgments of kingship are harsh. And the addition of גם, even before the latter ones, points to those who were before them, for they too did not rejoice in the old fool. Some interpret the second child as the generation coming after him. The meaning is that he saw the living walking under the sun — they are the people, their heirs who will stand in their place, just as they were with the first ones who were before them. Neither these nor those will rejoice in the world."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Resolved תוספ׳ as 'addition' (i.e., the grammatical particle גם) and עול׳ as abbreviation for עולם based on context."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:38.492680189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}